From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GraphicsEnvironment: per-app Qualcomm driver version in
 GL_VERSION

On this device GLES is provided by ANGLE on top of the turnip Vulkan
driver, and ANGLE's GL_VERSION is "OpenGL ES 3.2 (ANGLE 2.1 git hash:
...)". Unreal Engine enables Vulkan on Adreno 6xx only through its
Android_Adreno6xx_Vulkan device profile, which requires a minimum
Qualcomm driver version; of the values the profile selector reads, only
GL_VERSION can carry one ("V@0525.0"). Without it UE games select
Android_Adreno6xx, which disables Vulkan, and games that ship only Vulkan
shaders fail at startup with "Failed to initialize ShaderCodeLibrary ...
part of the Global shader library is missing".

ANGLE uses the ANGLE_GL_VERSION environment variable verbatim as
GL_VERSION when it is set and not empty. For the packages listed in the
global setting gaokun3_angle_gl_version_pkgs, set it to "OpenGL ES 3.2
V@0762.10 (ANGLE 2.1)" while the app's graphics environment is set up,
before any context becomes current. CoreSettingsObserver passes the
setting in coreSettings, as it does for the ANGLE per-app driver
selection, so apps do not read a hidden global setting themselves. The
device's settings app writes it; the list is empty by default.

It is per package because the value fixes the ES version at 3.2. That
matches the contexts ANGLE hands to apps through libEGL, but a Chromium
browser runs its own ANGLE on top of the system one and creates an ES 2.0
context for WebGL 1; with the same string set for every process
(debug.angle.gl_version) WebGL 1 fails to initialise in Edge ("maximum
transform feedback separate attribs is too small").

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific]
---
 core/java/android/os/GraphicsEnvironment.java | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../server/am/CoreSettingsObserver.java       |  3 ++
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/os/GraphicsEnvironment.java b/core/java/android/os/GraphicsEnvironment.java
index 92f42b1..4e93e06 100644
--- a/core/java/android/os/GraphicsEnvironment.java
+++ b/core/java/android/os/GraphicsEnvironment.java
@@ -75,6 +75,12 @@ public class GraphicsEnvironment {
     private static final String ANGLE_DRIVER_VERSION_NAME = "";
     private static final long ANGLE_DRIVER_VERSION_CODE = 0;
 
+    // Settings.Global key listing, comma separated, the packages that are told a Qualcomm-style
+    // driver version in GL_VERSION (setupAngleGlVersion()). CoreSettingsObserver passes it in
+    // coreSettings.
+    private static final String ANGLE_GL_VERSION_PKGS = "gaokun3_angle_gl_version_pkgs";
+    private static final String ANGLE_GL_VERSION = "OpenGL ES 3.2 V@0762.10 (ANGLE 2.1)";
+
     // System properties related to updatable graphics drivers.
     private static final String PROPERTY_GFX_DRIVER_PRODUCTION = "ro.gfx.driver.0";
     private static final String PROPERTY_GFX_DRIVER_PRERELEASE = "ro.gfx.driver.1";
@@ -156,6 +162,8 @@ public class GraphicsEnvironment {
         }
         Trace.traceEnd(Trace.TRACE_TAG_GRAPHICS);
 
+        setupAngleGlVersion(coreSettings, packageName);
+
         Trace.traceBegin(Trace.TRACE_TAG_GRAPHICS, "chooseDriver");
         if (!chooseDriver(context, coreSettings, pm, packageName, appInfoWithMetaData)) {
             if (!mShouldUseAngle) {
@@ -379,6 +387,39 @@ public class GraphicsEnvironment {
         return -1;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Report a Qualcomm-style driver version in ANGLE's GL_VERSION to the packages listed in
+     * ANGLE_GL_VERSION_PKGS.
+     *
+     * Unreal Engine enables Vulkan on Adreno only through device profiles that require a
+     * minimum Qualcomm driver version; of the values its profile selector reads, only
+     * GL_VERSION can carry one ("OpenGL ES 3.2 V@0525.0 ..."). ANGLE's own GL_VERSION carries
+     * none, so such games use GLES, and games that ship only Vulkan shaders fail at startup.
+     *
+     * ANGLE takes GL_VERSION verbatim from the ANGLE_GL_VERSION environment variable when it is
+     * not empty, read when a context first becomes current, which happens after this.
+     * GL_RENDERER and GL_VENDOR are unchanged. The value pins the ES version to 3.2, which is
+     * what ANGLE gives apps going through libEGL, but not what a Chromium browser's own ANGLE
+     * creates for WebGL 1: setting it for every process (debug.angle.gl_version) left WebGL 1
+     * unavailable in Edge. Hence a per-package opt-in, empty by default.
+     */
+    private static void setupAngleGlVersion(Bundle coreSettings, String packageName) {
+        if (coreSettings == null) {
+            return;
+        }
+        final List<String> packages =
+                getGlobalSettingsString(null, coreSettings, ANGLE_GL_VERSION_PKGS);
+        if (getPackageIndex(packageName, packages) < 0) {
+            return;
+        }
+        try {
+            android.system.Os.setenv("ANGLE_GL_VERSION", ANGLE_GL_VERSION, true);
+            Log.i(TAG, "ANGLE_GL_VERSION set for " + packageName);
+        } catch (android.system.ErrnoException e) {
+            Log.w(TAG, "Could not set ANGLE_GL_VERSION", e);
+        }
+    }
+
     private static ApplicationInfo getAppInfoWithMetadata(Context context,
                                                           PackageManager pm, String packageName) {
         ApplicationInfo ai;
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CoreSettingsObserver.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CoreSettingsObserver.java
index 99bd60f..d2403b0 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CoreSettingsObserver.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CoreSettingsObserver.java
@@ -126,6 +126,9 @@ class CoreSettingsObserver extends ContentObserver {
                 Settings.Global.ANGLE_GL_DRIVER_SELECTION_VALUES, String.class);
         sGlobalSettingToTypeMap.put(
                 Settings.Global.ANGLE_EGL_FEATURES, String.class);
+        // Packages told a Qualcomm-style driver version in ANGLE's GL_VERSION, see
+        // GraphicsEnvironment.setupAngleGlVersion().
+        sGlobalSettingToTypeMap.put("gaokun3_angle_gl_version_pkgs", String.class);
         sGlobalSettingToTypeMap.put(
                 Settings.Global.SHOW_ANGLE_IN_USE_DIALOG_BOX, String.class);
         sGlobalSettingToTypeMap.put(Settings.Global.ENABLE_GPU_DEBUG_LAYERS, int.class);
